# 09b round-17 distinguishing ablations of clean payload C13 (code tree = C11; one retained doc file)

Payload C13: 98d6cebcd5861e42c843fab65516829c8818bff8.
Each ablation changes exactly one behaviour in a detached worktree at C13, runs
packages/kernel/tests/*.test.ts against it, and is reverted before the next.
The exact edit script, its diff, the full run output and the parsed rejection are recorded
per ablation below. An ablation is REJECTED when named packet cases fail; that is what makes
those cases distinguishing rather than merely green.

XA/XB guard K11-R7-STATE-03 (install/restore direction). X1/X7/X3/X4/X8 re-prove the
own-data family guards (round-12 scripts, whose anchors are untouched by the K11-R12-ID-01
correction). X9 reintroduces one shared coordinator-global visible position for receipts
and refusals, and is rejected by the K11-R12-ID-01 nondisclosure oracle.

